<section id="section-01c">
  <div class="section-header">
    <span class="section-number">01c</span>
    <h2>Extended Colour Palette</h2>
  </div>

  <p class="section-intro">For complex charts and graphs requiring more than six categorical series, this extended palette provides thirteen additional colours. They are organised into six visual families so related hues can be paired or grouped intuitively. All colours have been tested against both the surface (#FEFEFE) and ink (#1E1E1E) for text legibility.</p>

  <div class="callout mb-xl">
    <strong>When to use the extended palette:</strong> Introduce these colours only when the data genuinely requires more than six distinct categories — for example, multi-country comparisons, complex flow diagrams, or demographic breakdowns. Avoid using them decoratively or to add visual interest. Extended colours should always appear alongside a legend; direct labelling is preferred where space allows.
  </div>

  <!-- ── WARM ACCENTS ─────────────────────── -->
  <p class="label-caps mb-sm">Warm Accents — Series 7–9</p>
  <div class="palette-grid mb-xl">
    <div class="swatch">
      <div class="swatch-color" style="background:#CC3E00;">
        <span class="swatch-label-top swatch-overlay--dark">Series 7</span>
      </div>
      <div class="swatch-info">
        <div class="swatch-name">Orange Dark</div>
        <div class="swatch-hex">#CC3E00</div>
        <div class="swatch-role">Deep burnt orange. Contrast vs surface 5.24 — passes AA for normal text with white labels. Use for emphasis against yellow fills, reference lines, and text annotations tied to warm data.</div>
      </div>
    </div>


    <div class="swatch">
      <div class="swatch-color" style="background:#F7BB49;">
        <span class="swatch-label-top badge--dim">Series 8</span>
      </div>
      <div class="swatch-info">
        <div class="swatch-name">Amber</div>
        <div class="swatch-hex">#F7BB49</div>
        <div class="swatch-role">Warm mid-yellow, bridges brand Yellow toward orange. Strong with dark ink labels. Contrast vs surface: 1.71 — use as fill only, not standalone text.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="swatch">
      <div class="swatch-color" style="background:#FFA97A;">
        <span class="swatch-label-top badge--dim">Series 9</span>
      </div>
      <div class="swatch-info">
        <div class="swatch-name">Peach</div>
        <div class="swatch-hex">#FFA97A</div>
        <div class="swatch-role">Warm coral, bridges brand Orange toward pink. Use with dark ink labels. Contrast vs surface: 1.86 — fill only, not standalone text.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>

  <!-- ── COOL / BLUE ─────────────────────── -->
  <p class="label-caps mb-sm">Cool / Blue — Series 10–11</p>
  <div class="palette-grid mb-xl">

    <div class="swatch">
      <div class="swatch-color" style="background:#008DC9;">
        <span class="swatch-label-top" style="background:rgba(0,0,0,0.15);color:#1E1E1E;">Series 10</span>
      </div>
      <div class="swatch-info">
        <div class="swatch-name">Sky Blue</div>
        <div class="swatch-hex">#008DC9</div>
        <div class="swatch-role">Strong mid-blue. Contrast vs surface 3.68 (passes AA for large text/UI). Use dark ink labels for small text. Pairs well with brand Yellow.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="swatch">
      <div class="swatch-color" style="background:#054694;">
        <span class="swatch-label-top swatch-overlay--white-mid">Series 11</span>
      </div>
      <div class="swatch-info">
        <div class="swatch-name">Navy</div>
        <div class="swatch-hex">#054694</div>
        <div class="swatch-role">Deep navy. Contrast vs surface 9.01 — white text passes AA. Excellent for dark-themed charts or as a strong anchor in multi-series layouts.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>

  <!-- ── GREEN / TEAL ────────────────────── -->
  <p class="label-caps mb-sm">Green / Teal — Series 12–13</p>
  <div class="palette-grid mb-xl">

    <div class="swatch">
      <div class="swatch-color" style="background:#40BF73;">
        <span class="swatch-label-top swatch-overlay--mid">Series 12</span>
      </div>
      <div class="swatch-info">
        <div class="swatch-name">Emerald</div>
        <div class="swatch-hex">#40BF73</div>
        <div class="swatch-role">Vivid mid-green. Contrast vs surface 2.33 — use dark ink labels on fills. Visually distinct from Teal (#00897B) in the core palette. Avoid pairing with Mint.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="swatch">
      <div class="swatch-color" style="background:#62D1BA;">
        <span class="swatch-label-top badge--dim">Series 13</span>
      </div>
      <div class="swatch-info">
        <div class="swatch-name">Mint</div>
        <div class="swatch-hex">#62D1BA</div>
        <div class="swatch-role">Light teal-green. Contrast vs surface 1.83 — fill only. Pairs well with Navy and Indigo for cool-toned multi-series. Do not pair directly with Emerald.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>

  <!-- ── PURPLE / VIOLET ─────────────────── -->
  <p class="label-caps mb-sm">Purple / Violet — Series 14–17</p>
  <div class="palette-grid mb-xl">

    <div class="swatch">
      <div class="swatch-color" style="background:#6363C0;">
        <span class="swatch-label-top swatch-overlay--white-mid">Series 14</span>
      </div>
      <div class="swatch-info">
        <div class="swatch-name">Indigo</div>
        <div class="swatch-hex">#6363C0</div>
        <div class="swatch-role">Medium indigo-purple. Contrast vs surface 5.11 — passes AA for normal text with white labels. Visually distinct from Navy. Strong anchor in cool palettes.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="swatch">
      <div class="swatch-color" style="background:#BD53BD;">
        <span class="swatch-label-top swatch-overlay--mid">Series 15</span>
      </div>
      <div class="swatch-info">
        <div class="swatch-name">Plum</div>
        <div class="swatch-hex">#BD53BD</div>
        <div class="swatch-role">Mid magenta-purple. Contrast vs surface 4.05 — borderline AA for large text. Use dark ink labels. Pairs well with Lilac for a purple graduation.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="swatch">
      <div class="swatch-color" style="background:#F5A1E7; ">
        <span class="swatch-label-top swatch-overlay--light">Series 16</span>
      </div>
      <div class="swatch-info">
        <div class="swatch-name">Pink</div>
        <div class="swatch-hex">#F5A1E7</div>
        <div class="swatch-role">Bright pastel pink. Contrast vs surface 1.87 — fills only. Pairs with Plum for a purple-pink graduation. Not for standalone data series without supplementary encoding.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="swatch">
      <div class="swatch-color" style="background:#D79EED;">
        <span class="swatch-label-top swatch-overlay--light">Series 17</span>
      </div>
      <div class="swatch-info">
        <div class="swatch-name">Lilac</div>
        <div class="swatch-hex">#D79EED</div>
        <div class="swatch-role">Soft lavender. Contrast vs surface 2.08 — fills only. Useful as a light tint paired with Indigo or Plum in sequential or area chart contexts.</div>
      </div>
    </div>


  </div>

  <!-- ── WARM NEUTRALS ─────────────────────── -->
  <p class="label-caps mb-sm">Warm Neutrals — Inactive &amp; background states</p>
  <div class="palette-grid mb-xl">

    <div class="swatch">
      <div class="swatch-color" style="background:#EEDEE0; border:1px solid #DDD;">
        <span class="swatch-label-top" style="background:rgba(0,0,0,0.06);color:#1E1E1E;">Neutral</span>
      </div>
      <div class="swatch-info">
        <div class="swatch-name">Blush Light</div>
        <div class="swatch-hex">#EEDEE0</div>
        <div class="swatch-role">Very light warm blush. Contrast vs surface 1.29 — background wash or row stripe only. Never use as a data fill that must be distinguished from the surface.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="swatch">
      <div class="swatch-color" style="background:#E5CCCE;">
        <span class="swatch-label-top" style="background:rgba(0,0,0,0.07);color:#1E1E1E;">Neutral</span>
      </div>
      <div class="swatch-info">
        <div class="swatch-name">Blush Mid</div>
        <div class="swatch-hex">#E5CCCE</div>
        <div class="swatch-role">Muted dusty rose. Contrast vs surface 1.50 — subtle fills and background bands. Pairs with Warm Grey for neutral data groupings. Not for active data series.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="swatch">
      <div class="swatch-color" style="background:#ACA1A1;">
        <span class="swatch-label-top badge--dim">Neutral</span>
      </div>
      <div class="swatch-info">
        <div class="swatch-name">Warm Grey</div>
        <div class="swatch-hex">#ACA1A1</div>
        <div class="swatch-role">Muted warm grey. Contrast vs surface 2.49 — use for inactive/deselected states, "other" category fills, or secondary axis lines. Do not use as a primary data series colour.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>

