  <hr class="section-divider">
  <p style="font-family:var(--font-display); font-weight:500; font-size:1.953rem; margin-bottom:0.5rem;">Palette Types</p>
  <p class="section-intro">Three palette types cover every data scenario. Choosing the right type is as important as choosing the right chart — using a sequential palette for categorical data introduces visual relationships that do not exist in the numbers.</p>

<div class="grid-3 mb-lg">

    <div class="card card--flush">
      <div class="card-header-pad">
        <div class="kicker kicker--yellow">TYPE A</div>
        <h3 class="card-title">Qualitative</h3>
        <p class="text-sm mb-xxs">For categorical data with no inherent order. Each colour is visually distinct with comparable brightness — no colour should appear more important than another.</p>
        <p class="mono-sm text-muted">USE FOR: product types, regions, named segments</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card-body-sm">
        <div class="row-sm"><div class="legend-swatch legend-swatch--yellow"></div><span class="mono-sm text-muted">Cat A — #FFCD00</span></div>
        <div class="row-sm"><div class="legend-swatch legend-swatch--orange"></div><span class="mono-sm text-muted">Cat B — #FF4F00</span></div>
        <div class="row-sm"><div style="width:28px;height:16px;background:#62D1BA;border-radius:2px;"></div><span class="mono-sm text-muted">Cat C — #62D1BA</span></div>
        <div class="row-sm"><div style="width:28px;height:16px;background:#054694;border-radius:2px;"></div><span class="mono-sm text-muted">Cat D — #054694</span></div>
        <div class="row-sm"><div style="width:28px;height:16px;background:#6363C0;border-radius:2px;"></div><span class="mono-sm text-muted">Cat E — #6363C0</span></div>
        <div class="row-sm"><div style="width:28px;height:16px;background:#ACA1A1;border-radius:2px;"></div><span class="mono-sm text-muted">Cat F — #ACA1A1</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card card--flush">
      <div class="card-header-pad">
        <div class="kicker kicker--yellow">TYPE B</div>
        <h3 class="card-title">Sequential</h3>
        <p class="text-sm mb-xxs">For numeric data with a natural order. A single hue progresses from light (low) to fully saturated (high). Use the 25–100% tint ramps from Section 01b.</p>
        <p class="mono-sm text-muted">USE FOR: heatmaps, ranked bars, intensity maps</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card-body-sm">
        <div class="row-sm"><div style="width:28px;height:16px;background:#FEF2BE;border:1px solid #e8e0a0;border-radius:2px;"></div><span class="mono-sm text-muted">#FEF2BE — Y25% Low</span></div>
        <div class="row-sm"><div style="width:28px;height:16px;background:#FEE67F;border-radius:2px;"></div><span class="mono-sm text-muted">#FEE67F — Y50%</span></div>
        <div class="row-sm"><div style="width:28px;height:16px;background:#FFD940;border-radius:2px;"></div><span class="mono-sm text-muted">#FFD940 — Y75%</span></div>
        <div class="row-sm"><div class="legend-swatch legend-swatch--yellow"></div><span class="mono-sm text-muted">#FFCD00 — Y100% High</span></div>
        <div class="rule-thin"></div>
        <div class="row-sm"><div style="width:28px;height:16px;background:#E5CCCE;border:1px solid #e8c0a8;border-radius:2px;"></div><span class="mono-sm text-muted">#FED2BE — O25% Low</span></div>
        <div class="row-sm"><div style="width:28px;height:16px;background:#FFA97A;border-radius:2px;"></div><span class="mono-sm text-muted">#FEA67F — O50%</span></div>
        <div class="row-sm"><div style="width:28px;height:16px;background:#E8A832;border-radius:2px;"></div><span class="mono-sm text-muted">#FF7B40 — O75%</span></div>
        <div class="row-sm"><div class="legend-swatch legend-swatch--orange"></div><span class="mono-sm text-muted">#FF4F00 — O100% High</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card card--flush">
      <div class="card-header-pad">
        <div class="kicker kicker--yellow">TYPE C</div>
        <h3 class="card-title">Divergent</h3>
        <p class="text-sm mb-xxs">Two sequential scales meeting at a neutral midpoint. For data with a meaningful centre — where values above and below zero carry opposite significance.</p>
        <p class="mono-sm text-muted">USE FOR: above/below target, positive/negative change, sentiment</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card-body-sm">
        <div class="palette-bar">
          <div style="flex:1;background:#F7BB49;"></div>
          <div style="flex:1;background:#E8A832;"></div>
          <div style="flex:1;background:#FFA97A;"></div>
          <div style="flex:1;background:#E0E0E0;"></div>
          <div style="flex:1;background:#FEE67F;"></div>
          <div style="flex:1;background:#FFD940;"></div>
          <div style="flex:1;background:#FFCD00;"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="row-between mono-xxs text-muted">
          <span>Negative</span><span>#E0E0E0</span><span>Positive</span>
        </div>
        <p style="font-size:0.75rem; color:var(--ink-mid); line-height:1.5; margin-bottom:0.5rem;">Orange anchors negative; Yellow anchors positive; Rule grey as neutral midpoint.</p>
        <div class="note-yellow"><strong>Avoid red/green</strong> — culturally ambiguous and inaccessible for colour-blind users.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>
